Added a parameter to disables/ignores the endpoints detected in the SD. This implementation is related to the issue #1061 .

In a JS application this parameter (`ignoreSparqlEndpointFromServiceDescription`) should be passed in the source list such as: 
```js
const result = await this.queryEngine.query(query, {
    sources: [
        { value: 'https://dbpedia.org/sparql', ignoreSparqlEndpointFromServiceDescription: true},
        { value: 'https://query.wikidata.org/sparql, type: 'sparql'}
    ]
});
```

Using the command line I chose to use the `+` character preceding the url that should be used without accessing the SD. Then:
```
> comunica-sparql +https://fragments.dbpedia.org/2016-04/en \
    sparql@https://query.wikidata.org/sparql \
    "SELECT * WHERE { ?s ?p ?o } LIMIT 100"
```

Previously, we processed cameras sequentially in a loop:
```rust
loop {
    let response = recv_string().await;
    get_responding_addr(response).await;
    ...
}
```

And now, `get_responding_addr()` is called concurrently for each camera as soon as responses arrive.

This PR is a step towards simplifying and getting better performance in esv-intersection.

Previously we created a absolute positioned HTML element and created a PIXI Application inside the component; Now we pass in a PIXI Application in the constructor of the Layer class, and achieve the layering effect by using a PIXI Display Object.

```
// PixiLayer.ts
constructor(ctx: Application | PixiRenderApplication, id?: string, options?: LayerOptions) {
    super(id, options);

    this._ctx = ctx;

    this._container = new Container();
    this._ctx.stage.addChild(this._container);
  }
```

